# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: CI runs on ubuntu-latest while development happens on
# Windows, where git's `core.autocrlf` is often `true`.  Without a pin, the
# stored line endings depend on each contributor's local git config, which
# produces whole-file diffs when two people disagree and can break shell
# scripts or workflow steps on the Linux runner.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Platform-specific helpers keep their native endings.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never line-ending convert binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
